---
title: Side-by-side columns
---

# Side-by-side columns

`\{% columns %}` places its children in equal-width columns, side by side.
Each column is either a list item (`*`) or a blank-line-separated block; the
`gap` attribute (points) sets the space between them. Render with
`--assets-root examples` so the swatch images resolve.

## Two images — list form

{% columns %}
* ![](swatch.png)
* ![](swatch.svg)
{% /columns %}

## Three columns, wider gap — block form

{% columns gap=28 %}
![](swatch.png)

![](swatch.svg)

![](swatch.png)
{% /columns %}

## Per-column captions

Put a `\{% caption %}` and its image in one list item, separated by a blank
line, so they stay distinct blocks and the caption attaches to the image:

{% columns %}
* {% caption %}Raster swatch{% /caption %}

  ![](swatch.png)

* {% caption %}Vector swatch{% /caption %}

  ![](swatch.svg)
{% /columns %}
